// Two DIFFERENT rounding contracts never mix silently: picking one would be a
// decision nobody wrote down.
//
// This fixture used to say "not even with none" — a contract mixing with a plain
// Decimal was refused too. That was relaxed in v0.0.86: addition never rounds, so
// one contract and no contract leaves exactly one answer, and the old rule meant a
// contract could only be declared where money entered the program. See
// tests/pass/contract_widening.bx for what is now allowed.
let a: Decimal<2, RoundHalfEven> = 1.00;
let b: Decimal<2, RoundHalfUp> = 2.00;
print(a + b);
